Chekhov Deep Writing is a multi-license distribution.

1. Original code in this release is licensed under Apache License 2.0.
   See LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt.

2. Project-authored research cards, workflow documentation, mechanism cards,
   and other original explanatory materials are licensed under Creative
   Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0), by the repository owner.
   See LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt.

3. Russian Wikisource transcriptions and their derived clean/reading files are
   distributed under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
   (CC BY-SA 4.0), with the underlying Chekhov works in the public domain.
   Attribution, fixed revision URLs, and hashes are in corpus/source-registry.csv
   and corpus/corpus-manifest.json. See LICENSES/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt.

4. Project Gutenberg research-source files retain the Project Gutenberg terms
   embedded in those files. They are included only in the research snapshot.

5. Modern Chinese published translations are not licensed by this release and
   are not included. Bibliographic target records do not grant text rights.

Where a file carries a more specific notice, that notice controls.


Public writing foundation added in cluster 1.1.0:
The separate derived writing foundation documents are CC BY-NC 4.0.
The Human Writing-derived checker remains MIT. Existing material retains
its preceding license; see LICENSES/WRITING-FOUNDATION-NOTICE.md for file scope.
